Technics SX-KN7000 floppy disks.

These carry the KN7000's "Initial Data" / custom-data: the user-data sets the
instrument installs on a front-panel data load, which populate the custom-data
flash (IC21) and the battery-backed user memory.  Each is available as a
self-extracting PC archive that writes its payload onto a blank FAT12 HD diskette,
and physical diskettes are known to exist; who prepared or distributed them is
unclear (not necessarily official releases).  No original diskette has been
dumped, so these images are faithful reconstructions built from the archives' own
files, which a dump of an original could supersede.
-->
